  "body": "**Link to problem area**: https://spec.matrix.org/v1.7/client-server-api/#recovery-key\r\n\r\n**Issue**\r\n\r\nThe spec uses \"recovery key\" to refer to the [private part of a key backup key](https://spec.matrix.org/v1.7/client-server-api/#recovery-key).\r\n\r\nOur clients (in both code and UI) use \"recovery key\" to mean a 4S key, which is a [completely different sort of key](https://spec.matrix.org/v1.7/client-server-api/#msecret_storagev1aes-hmac-sha2) (although they do use the same base58 algorithm for presentation to the user: [4S](https://spec.matrix.org/v1.7/client-server-api/#key-representation), [key backup](https://spec.matrix.org/v1.7/client-server-api/#recovery-key)).\r\n\r\nI propose that the spec avoid the term \"recovery key\" altogether, since it is so overloaded, and instead just say \"key-backup decryption key\" or something suitably long-winded but explicit. ",
